76290845871, 0.00986313633620739, 0.023400159552693367, 0.00017009343719109893, 0.005787416826933622, -0.024944862350821495, -0.026406068354845047, -0.026656560599803925, -0.025362350046634674, -0.01285860687494278, -0.001412933343090117, 0.0191417895257473, 0.0015629678964614868, 0.037511229515075684, -0.004748917184770107, 0.012044507078826427, 0.011345216073095798, -0.027324538677930832, 0.04085112735629082, -0.03216738998889923, 0.0006454744143411517, 0.012211501598358154, -0.005135092884302139, 0.04855376482009888, 0.0031624657567590475, -0.029349353164434433, 0.005043767858296633, -0.002665395149961114, -0.004884600639343262, -0.004921130836009979, 0.03661363199353218, 0.006251871585845947, -0.0009589159744791687, -0.022252069786190987, -0.004013095982372761, -0.013683144003152847, -0.0198723915964365, 0.006225778255611658, -0.010019693523645401, -0.013443089090287685, 0.030100829899311066, 0.0035564694553613663, -0.0037469479721039534, 0.028514377772808075]], "input": ["FASSNACHT M:Fassnacht M is a prominent contributor to the European Society of Endocrinology guidelines concerning adrenal incidentalomas. He is actively involved in the management guidelines for these conditions and participates in endocrinology research. Additionally, Fassnacht M is recognized as one of the authors of the article addressing the management of adrenal incidentalomas within the European Society of Endocrinology guidelines.", "BANCOS I:Bancos I is a significant contributor to the management guidelines for adrenal incidentalomas, emphasizing clinical practice in the field of endocrinology. Additionally, Bancos I is recognized as an author of the European Society of Endocrinology guidelines specifically addressing the management of adrenal incidentalomas.", "NEWELL-PRICE J:Newell-Price J is a prominent contributor to the European Society of Endocrinology guidelines concerning adrenal incidentalomas. This individual is recognized for their significant research in adrenal disorders and has played a key role in developing management guidelines for these conditions. As an author of the European Society of Endocrinology guidelines on the management of adrenal incidentalomas, Newell-Price J has contributed valuable insights and expertise to the field.", "SAHDEV A:Sahdev A is a notable contributor to the European Society of Endocrinology guidelines concerning adrenal incidentalomas. He has played a significant role in the development of management guidelines for these conditions, demonstrating his involvement in the field of clinical endocrinology. As an author of the European Society of Endocrinology guidelines on the management of adrenal incidentalomas, Sahdev A's expertise and contributions are integral to the understanding and treatment of this area in endocrinology.", "SÍNDROME DE CUSHING SUBCLÍNICO:El síndrome de Cushing subclínico es un estado transitorio que puede revertir y que puede progresar a un síndrome de Cushing manifiesto, aunque su evolución no está clara y es poco frecuente.", "HORMONAS SEXUALES:HORMONAS SEXUALES, or sex hormones, are crucial hormones that regulate the development and functioning of reproductive organs. This group includes hormones such as FSH (follicle-stimulating hormone), LH (luteinizing hormone), and testosterone, as well as androgens and estrogens. The measurement of sex hormones is particularly important in clinical scenarios where there is a suspicion of adrenal carcinoma, as their secretion by a benign adenoma is quite rare. In cases of adrenal incidentalomas, where there is a clinical suspicion of malignancy, it is essential to evaluate the potential secretion of sex hormones by adrenal tumors. Thus, the assessment of these hormones plays a significant role in the diagnosis and management of conditions related to the adrenal glands and reproductive health.", "YOUNG WF, JR:Young WF, Jr es el autor del artículo sobre el incidentaloma adrenal en UpToDate, que proporciona información actualizada sobre el tema.", "ALD/ARP:The aldosterone/renin plasma activity ratio is a test performed to assess adrenal function, particularly in cases of primary hyperaldosteronism.", "EPLERENONA:Eplerenone is another aldosterone antagonist similar to spironolactone, which also requires withdrawal before testing for accurate interpretation.", "SECRECIÓN DE HORMONAS SEXUALES:The secretion of sex hormones by adrenal tumors is rare, typically associated with malignant conditions.", "GUIAS:Guidelines refer to the recommendations for the management and follow-up of adrenal incidentalomas, which may vary based on initial imaging characteristics.", "ADRENAL INCIDENTALOMA:ADRENAL INCIDENTALOMA is a medical condition characterized by the discovery of an adrenal mass that is not associated with symptoms of adrenal dysfunction. This condition typically arises incidentally during imaging studies conducted for unrelated reasons, and it does not present any clinical symptoms related to adrenal hormone overproduction or deficiency.", "BANKOS I:Bankos I is a contributor to the European Society of Endocrinology guidelines on adrenal incidentalomas.", "TAC ABDOMINAL:TAC abdominal, also known as a computed tomography (CT) scan of the abdomen, is a diagnostic imaging procedure utilized primarily to identify incidentalomas in the adrenal glands and to detect masses or abnormalities within the abdominal region. This imaging technique has been instrumental in confirming diagnoses, such as pancreatic adenocarcinoma, by providing detailed images that help in the assessment of various conditions affecting the abdominal organs.", "DHEA:Dehydroepiandrosterone (DHEA) is a weak androgen hormone produced by the adrenal glands. It plays a significant role in the body's hormonal balance and is often measured in the evaluation of adrenal function. DHEA can activate certain steroid receptors, albeit with lower affinity. In cases of aromatase deficiency, DHEA levels may be elevated, which can contribute to virilization symptoms. Additionally, DHEA is relevant in the study of adrenal incidentalomas, as it is an important marker in assessing adrenal health. It is noteworthy that DHEA can be converted into more potent androgens, such as testosterone, further emphasizing its role in the endocrine system.", "POTASSIUM:Potassium is an essential mineral and electrolyte that plays a crucial role in various bodily functions. It is commonly measured in blood tests to assess adrenal function and other health conditions. Found abundantly in fruits, vegetables, and other foods, potassium is vital for heart health and may aid in controlling blood pressure, particularly in individuals with high sodium intake. \n\nIn addition to its cardiovascular benefits, potassium influences kidney health and the formation of kidney stones. It helps regulate fluid balance in the body, making it important for overall health. However, potassium intake may need to be restricted in the diets of certain patients, especially those with chronic kidney disease, to prevent complications such as hyperkalemia. For patients without diuresis undergoing treatment with ACE inhibitors, potassium intake should not exceed 1 mEq/kg/day. Consequently, potassium levels are closely monitored and managed in dietary recommendations for individuals with kidney issues to ensure their health and well-being."], "parameters": {"model": "text-embedding-3-small", "temperature": 0.0, "frequency_penalty": null, "presence_penalty": null, "top_p": 1.0, "max_tokens": 4000, "n": 1}, "history": null}